From 9a1ccbd6c6881184d41a5859894df41988b2b3ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:46:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] audit3 H9: read_files works on pcemu's image itself, not
 a 1.47 MB copy each time

disk_file and the other read_files callers copied the whole floppy with
bytes() first, at every poll (every 0.05 sim s at 49 sites); read_files
only slices the root and each file's clusters, so it takes the bytearray
as it is. Snapshots taken to compare later keep their copies. (Left as
they are: claude_kernel.py's, another row's file, and test_kernel's MS-DOS
probe tests, H7's.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GRD5wiUMCniTFB6AGgxU9p
